<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey's deadly factory blast: 'Investing in safety costs more than letting people die'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3a4b98f70880a575974477e312b45b0321f8eea2bc41c2de3dec74a1d9815e1</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:43:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T17:28:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-factory-blast-turkey-izmir--11e9146de7c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-factory-blast-turkey-izmir" /><summary type="html">An explosion at a steel factory on November 9 in Turkey's Aliaga, near Izmir, killed 19 people. This tragedy follows several others and highlights the issues surrounding workers’ safety in Turkey, our Observers say. They also condemn the repressive responses from the government and the company.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Moldova launches national preparedness campaign after drone incursions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0874ac1baaa022feaf368fc34f68c183e5dce7a6c29f2e57fe857f6cbbe7d4df</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:43:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T16:34:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/moldova-launches-national-preparedness-campaign-after-drone-incursions--b8c5b821eb8d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/moldova-launches-national-preparedness-campaign-after-drone-incursions" /><summary type="html">Moldova is urging its citizens to prepare for emergencies as the war in neighbouring Ukraine brings new risks across its border. The “Moldova Ready” campaign, launched in Chisinau, includes a display of the remains of a drone carrying 52kg of explosives after it crashed in the country last month. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Kremlin declines comment on reports 700,000 Russian soldiers killed in Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1b190d5cc275c6f5e9c747869c1d24c39dfd649b085c9e8753f2d6d32c2bf8e3</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:14:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-kremlin-declines-comment-reports-700-000-russian-soldiers-killed-ukraine-war--97c7af478f38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-kremlin-declines-comment-reports-700-000-russian-soldiers-killed-ukraine-war" /><summary type="html">Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov on Wednesday declined to comment on reports in Russian and international news outlets that around 700,000 Russian soldiers have been killed in the Ukraine war so far. The reports were based on hacked data from Russia's official statistics agency. Peskov said only the defence ministry can disclose figures and told reporters "not to pay attention to any other data".</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Surprise Eurostar strike cancels London, Paris and Brussels trains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18d6d31f0fe70eaa24792a9e56d1236197e87fdb98d38dc4ed89dd99f4b9bb72</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:02:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-surprise-eurostar-strike-cancels-london-paris-and-brussels-trains--87744ac1110c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-surprise-eurostar-strike-cancels-london-paris-and-brussels-trains" /><summary type="html">Several Eurostar trains connecting London, Paris and Brussels were cancelled in a surprise strike on Wednesday. The train operator did not specify who exactly was striking or the reasons why.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Two Libyan soldiers killed in Ukrainian attack on Russian vessels in Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c479bb3c2b3fed28863aa9ee60e3e079b954a9a84acd38285af365b2280f420</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T03:46:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-live-two-libyan-soldiers-killed-in-ukrainian-attack-on-russian-vessels-in-benghazi--3e3be77f4806.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-live-two-libyan-soldiers-killed-in-ukrainian-attack-on-russian-vessels-in-benghazi" /><summary type="html">Two Libyan soldiers have died from injuries sustained in an attack, claimed by Ukraine, on Russian ships near Benghazi, a senior figure in the administration in eastern Libya said late on Tuesday. Members of the European Parliament will convene in Strasbourg on Wednesday to discuss "Europe’s role and capacity to protect the international order and secure a just and lasting peace for Ukraine". Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine seeks €115 billion in foreign aid for 2027, Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01d37ebaad83ca117d8e916f57bbe6410f66130cf8492c0e7fb1123a8f849f11</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T01:19:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-ukraine-seeks-_115-billion-in-foreign-aid-for-2027-zelensky-says--06c01a5e24b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261125-ukraine-seeks-%E2%82%AC115-billion-in-foreign-aid-for-2027-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukraine will need €115 billion in external financing next year to sustain its economy and war effort against Russia, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday, adding that Kyiv had secured commitments for about €90 billion from the European Union.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russian nuclear satellites plan 'foolhardy', expert says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eaf0837f53bafff9128522242cc3b7cdb622a0e96f3bdd7bdb028e6222d227da</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T20:31:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says--a17887817d5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-nuclear-satellites-plan-foolhardy-expert-says" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. Speaking to FRANCE 24, Dafydd Townley, Senior Teaching Fellow in International Security at the University of Portsmouth, says that the alleged plan would be "foolhardy because the impact would be indiscriminate, they wouldn't be able to choose only Western or non-Russian satellites".</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian losses on Ukrainian front top 700,000 including missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d5175f0d8594e449f2a1234c912a6388073dfcd0199be4aac1586488bf324c</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T19:22:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing--6a745520bcf6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-losses-on-ukrainian-front-top-700-000-including-missing" /><summary type="html">New analysis of leaked Russian government data suggests more than 700,000 Russian soldiers have died in the war against Ukraine. Independent Russian media outlets have updated their estimates of Moscow's military casualties, including soldiers missing on the frontline, after Belarusian and Ukrainian hackers obtained figures from the Russian statistics agency. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia's war on Ukraine: 'Both sides are prepared to operate outside of the conflict zone'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71f0bb454d8938d49e21a9c6a3fa9aa50a682458cb247a034010bf2936c5bfad</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T17:26:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone--766d3b319486.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-war-on-ukraine-both-sides-are-prepared-to-operate-outside-of-the-conflict-zone" /><summary type="html">Charli James is pleased to welcome Gavin Hall, Teaching Fellow in Political Science, and International Security at the University of Strathclyde. Hall examines recent Russian and Ukrainian operations beyond the main conflict zone, the conditions necessary for a negotiated settlement and the implications of diminishing direct US military support for Ukraine. “Both sides are prepared to operate beyond the main battleground and outside of the conflict zone,” he explains. Hall discusses why both sides want to negotiate from a position of strength and the conditions under which a “mutually hurting stalemate” could lead to a negotiated settlement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Putin says Ukraine still hits Russian oil plants despite Trump's requests to stop</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20ed5a5645739b074444aa2078e6f72c68705a62f51d086fdf0d548ab3261610</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:50:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters--e55baa58ddf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-live-tripoli-demands-explanation-from-kyiv-for-striking-russian-ships-in-libyan-waters" /><summary type="html">Ukraine continues attacks on Russian oil refineries despite requests from US President ​Donald Trump to ‌withhold them, Russian leader Vladimir Putin said Tuesday, pledging to ⁠retaliate. Kyiv has said it would not stop targeting Russian energy targets until Moscow had done the same. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky urges four-way peace talks with Russia, Europe and US 'as soon as possible'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43b4e07cd0c74f4ba98297d82efc7f022c94f9f08d1e4c0da52dd0f4b5dcf1c9</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T00:30:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible--354e3c5e6ad8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261124-zelensky-urges-four-way-peace-talks-with-russia-europe-and-us-as-soon-as-possible" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is calling for a new round of negotiations involving Ukraine, Russia, the United States and European leaders, saying Kyiv is ready to meet as early as Tuesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>NATO vows space defence after Russia nuclear satellite report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46212584cdad6ab6909c10d4f503da5db0a65f85278331f0cca36cccf331b3b3</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:33:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report--b818d8d38eb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nato-vows-space-defence-after-russia-nuclear-satellite-report" /><summary type="html">NATO chief Mark Rutte said Monday the alliance would defend against threats in space when asked about German media reports that Russia may be preparing to launch a nuclear-armed satellite. The media reports, citing unnamed German military and BND spy agency sources, said Moscow was thought to be planning such a launch in the coming weeks, giving it the capability to destroy other satellites. FRANCE 24's Laurent Berstecher reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd15502ebc9c1d40c40d5f5c7cd9f4e2932e559e3b4fa332a0c6c7c2b1acc80</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--b335b8ca1842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261123-a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: 'A war of unmanned machines, AI and total transparency of the battlefield'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8adb09184945de3e75bfb16c5a260fd784cefa899d6fe5fe94333efc57056d76</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T21:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield--4945328f5666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/a-war-of-unmanned-machines-ai-and-total-transparency-of-the-battlefield" /><summary type="html">Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that today's war in Ukraine "is a war of unmanned machines, AI, total transparency of the battlefield, mass drone attacks and long-range weapons, and this means we have to rethink how to protect human beings".</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya's east seeks UN probe into claims Ukrainian military present in west</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd2252ac1b20ebd7bedb62eba41411b60efdd7a17ba62c60a3e4153b615641a2</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west--6cb055560ea5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/libya-s-east-seeks-un-probe-into-claims-ukrainian-military-present-in-west" /><summary type="html">Authorities in divided Libya's east called on Monday for the United Nations to investigate claims that Ukrainian forces were present in the country's west, as they lodged a complaint over Ukrainian attacks on two Russian ships off Benghazi. The strikes on Sunday, claimed by Kyiv, come as Ukraine steps up strikes against Russia far from the front lines of their war. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims it sank Russian warship off Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1335987e61b434f0740997d307b5db836b953a749d86f258e07fe423fd0f4bd2</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T19:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya--1e8645cf71f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-claims-it-sank-russian-warship-off-libya" /><summary type="html">Ukraine on Monday claimed it was behind strikes on two Russian vessels off Libya, including one that sank a modern warship, in the latest spillover from Moscow's invasion. The attacks on Sunday near the Libyan port of Benghazi come at a time when Ukraine has stepped up its daring strikes against Russia far from the frontlines in retaliation for Moscow's deadly invasion. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Finland summons Russian ambassador after suspected airspace violation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:287ab237d3985421b6f73a511dad74c950d4414ed8489e1fd4b55ddce77ae679</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:50:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation--777165c768bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-finland-summons-russian-ambassador-after-suspected-airspace-violation" /><summary type="html">Finland on Monday said it had summoned Russia's ambassador over a suspected violation of Finnish airspace by a Russian helicopter and after a Ukrainian drone strike on a Russian cargo ship located in the Gulf of Finland in recent days. Helsinki also condemned Moscow's escalating strikes on civilian targets in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>12,000 evacuated from Don Toliver concert after unknown substance sickens fans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d96b09dc7346cbc823567652d5d52435748b78cd660ec6d222e1f329d4d386f9</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:46:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans--c4a2bcadc8d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-12-000-evacuated-from-don-toliver-concert-after-unknown-substance-sickens-fans" /><summary type="html">More than 12,000 fans were evacuated from a concert by American rapper Don Toliver and over 80 were treated by medics after an unknown irritant was released in the crowd, authorities in the English city of Manchester said Monday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine claims strikes on Russian ships off Libyan coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a15c17dd656e89574ac1b3f2a258eee4ec20858a038b872ecf7139b72834f58f</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast--c6da19d54d8f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261123-ukraine-claims-strikes-on-russian-ships-off-libyan-coast" /><summary type="html">Ukraine claimed responsibility on Monday for attacks on two Russian vessels off the coast of Libya the previous day. Here is what we know about the operation, claimed by President Volodymyr Zelensky shortly after the United Nations called for an investigation into the strikes.</summary></entry><entry><title>Libya demands answers from Kyiv over drone attack on Russian ships off Benghazi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2754e8c21871c3671b406d9f894554b110327c8423052973876dd6fb7ac8251a</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T06:10:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says--3314f31f0d59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261123-live-russian-strikes-kill-at-least-15-people-in-kyiv-region-ukraine-says" /><summary type="html">Libya's Tripoli-based government on Monday condemned Ukraine's strikes on two Russian vessels near the eastern city of Benghazi carried out by Ukraine on Sunday. It demanded an explanation from Kyiv, warning that Libya would not be dragged into the war between Russia and Ukraine. Read our live blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Burnham, 'Brejoin' &amp; the ghosts of Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27707729c5729cd45b0eddf5b9f1511bd946c526f4cd4b1e98ec6950b77609b0</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T19:37:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit--b3f015196424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261122-burnham-brejoin-the-ghosts-of-brexit" /><summary type="html">"The people of Britain have spoken, and the answer is: we are out." Those were the words of David Dimbleby at 4:40am on June 24, 2016, as the Brexit referendum result became clear. But nearly a decade on, is Britain changing its mind? Prime Minister Andy Burnham has reopened talks with Brussels, exploring options for a closer relationship with the EU. The move has, however, drawn criticism from key figures behind Brexit, including Theresa May and Boris Johnson. What is driving this rethink and where might it lead? FRANCE 24's Gavin Lee speaks to John McTernan, veteran Labour strategist and former adviser to Tony Blair.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Europe sees new protests over rising costs, inequality and public services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f779439fe5d88ab06f1f1c5bc775e9cb89220a5240e819ea27ed1feafec15056</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T09:41:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services--a1d144e53fad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-sees-new-protests-over-rising-costs-inequality-and-public-services" /><summary type="html">Sunday marks the third consecutive day of protests across Europe, following large demonstrations on Friday and smaller rallies on Saturday, from Portugal to France. The protests have largely focused on the rising cost of living and access to affordable housing. In France, demonstrations have now taken place for six weekends in a row. Ophelie Jacobson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian rescuers search for survivors in rubble after Russian attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185963357f0556cc78353eb11c6b97fe965ee6c98657c33a2fcff4f2f4367a95</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T06:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship--98ee191af9fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261122-live-finland-says-war-spilling-over-after-baltic-sea-drone-strike-on-russian-cargo-ship" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian rescue teams on Sunday searched for survivors in the rubble of a collapsed residential building in Dymer, in the Kyiv region, after a Russian drone strike, which killed two people and wounded four others. Meanwhile, Finland warned the war was "spilling over" after a drone set fire to a Russian cargo ship in the Baltic Sea Saturday. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia agreement sees the light after ten years of negotiations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01f3dfe2f8319e496731d380b39278c16b9b3dcbe31ad90e522e4ccc2751195b</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T22:23:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations--6b9c7be2271c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261121-eu-indonesia-agreement-sees-the-light-after-ten-years-of-negotiations" /><summary type="html">The European Union and Indonesia have signed a major trade deal, ten years after talks began.The agreement removes almost all tariffs between the EU and Southeast Asia's biggest economy: 98.5 per cent of them. For Europe, it means access to a market of 280 million people and a steadier supply of nickel for batteries. For Indonesia, easier exports of palm oil, textiles and footwear, and it arrives just before its current EU trade preferences end on the 1st of January. To discuss the deal Airlangga Hartarto, Coordinating Minister for Economic Affairs in Indonesia joined us on the programme.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia attacks Zelensky's hometown, Ukraine reaffirms wish to join NATO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:000afd0df7e691a35a10a59d8077946f61d2dcf929d51f34e4bfb93888cfc197</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:56:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato--7bb8a856bfbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-russia-attacks-zelensky-s-hometown-ukraine-reaffirms-wish-to-join-nato" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO, following proposals to provide Kyiv with security guarantees similar to those of the military alliance.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia launches ballistic missile attack on Zelensky's hometown in central Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b553c8eea4ee4ce7105ac3b78297bb2437480aa4351aef084fe3b5f4f5457f48</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T19:55:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine--9ccdbee28248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-launches-ballistic-missile-attack-on-zelensky-s-hometown-in-central-ukraine" /><summary type="html">A Russian ballistic missile attack on President Volodymyr Zelensky’s hometown in central Ukraine on Saturday killed two people and wounded dozens. Hours later, Zelensky reiterated his country's determination to join NATO. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5651baa90aea88fed148a6d07e5d0b48b79f090a800309efdc59038b2d0646dd</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T18:02:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--6ddedb55210c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after ​being hit by drones in the Baltic Sea on Saturday and drifted into Finnish waters. Reporting from Kyiv, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg notes that the ship is affiliated with a major Russian military logistics company. While Ukrainian authorities typically neither confirm nor deny responsibility, analysts cite a clear motive for the targeting, Cragg explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe636a668ab0927c0acec44878e95da01dc517799ef459f4fcbe1cdee6e382a3</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:35:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--c7c9c4110e34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into the country's ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ccfa0a71065bfefaa3c4ec601141f4cccd0cad0262eff877d6eb7efe8ef33ac</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes--a6892ead2cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes" /><summary type="html">A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d6319b9128cc2b302e73f886fd077cd67fd1db374e684883e6ca5227c573b5b</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:32:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen--dca3e06988cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
